.TH ASTRUM 1 "" "Astrum" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
astrum \- a persistent terminal with tabs, mouse support and a built\-in AI agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B astrum
.RB [ \-s
.IR SESSION ]
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B astrum
runs inside the terminal you already use. It shows your own shell with a tab
bar above it and a status bar below, keeps your shells running in the
background when the window is closed, and has an agent that works in the same
shell you do.
.PP
Run with no command, it attaches to the session, starting it first if it is
not running. Everything on screen can be clicked;
.B \(eq menu
in the status bar lists every action with the key that does the same. The
prefix key is
.B Ctrl+B
unless changed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B attach
Attach to the session, starting it if needed. This is what happens when no
command is given.
.TP
.B ls
List running sessions, and stopped ones whose tabs would come back.
.TP
.BR kill " [" \-\-all "] [" \-\-forget ]
Stop a session and close its shells. Its tabs come back the next time it is
started, unless
.B \-\-forget
is given.
.B \-\-all
stops every session.
.TP
.BR config " [" \-\-init ]
Show where the config file is.
.B \-\-init
writes a commented starter file there.
.TP
.B themes
List the color themes, the built\-in ones and your own.
.TP
.B keys
List what Astrum's keys do, with the keys each action has now.
.TP
.B reload
Have a running session read its settings, providers and keys again, passing
along the key variables of the shell it is run from.
.TP
.BR service " " install | uninstall | status
Run the session under the system's service manager (launchd on macOS, the
systemd user manager on Linux), so that it starts at login and is started
again if it stops.
.B install \-\-print
shows what would be written without doing it.
.TP
.BR completions " " bash | zsh | fish
Print a completion script for that shell.
.TP
.B man
Print this manual page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-session " " \fINAME\fR
The session to act on. Each session has its own tabs. The default is
.BR default .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/astrum/config.toml
Settings. Read again whenever it is saved.
.TP
.I ~/.config/astrum/state.toml
What was chosen inside Astrum; takes the place of the config file for
those settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/astrum/
Saved sessions, saved conversations, and the shell integration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ASTRUM_CONFIG_DIR, ASTRUM_DATA_DIR, ASTRUM_RUNTIME_DIR
Other places for the settings, the saved data, and the session sockets.
.TP
.B ASTRUM_CLIPBOARD_TOOL, ASTRUM_OPEN_TOOL
The program copied text is handed to, and the one a link is opened with;
.B none
for neither.
.SH SEE ALSO
The README and the changelog, at
.UR https://github.com/robert\-mcdermott/astrum
the project's page
.UE .
